    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648-a2">

                <pb facs="0618" n="1352" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1352"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure to inclosure in No.
                    684.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral Selfridge to Mr. Herbert.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. San Francisco</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Marseilles
                                France</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward to the
                    Department the following copies of reports on the situation in Asia Minor,
                    received from Commander Charles O’Neil, U. S. N., commanding the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead:</hi> Report dated October 24, 1895, with two
                    inclosures; report dated October 30, 1895.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos O. Selfridge</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral, U. S. N.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
